{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_011CdsYyv69GceerMtGwLRJp","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01PTnjy4KMj4dNTzJTMQquQ9","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/claude-0/-home-user-creator-0/113f7cc5-237e-5d6a-8867-a97fd89c58dd/scratchpad/e6/e6-t07/primary/exec-ws/ea-analysis.md","content":"# E-A analysis — render.md vs render.py on the full probe set (e6-t07)\n\nScope: every behavior exercised by the ten probes in `package/artifacts/probes.json`\n(indices 0–9), mapped to what `render.md` prescribes and compared against the\nsemantics of `render.py`. This analysis may freely consult all three artifacts\n(E-A carries no authorship restriction).\n\n## Reference semantics\n\n`render.py` computes `re.sub(r\"\\{\\{([a-z]+)\\}\\}\", lambda m: str(ctx.get(m.group(1), \"\")), t)`.\nBecause the replacement is a callable, its return value is inserted literally\n(no backreference processing), and `re.sub` performs a single left-to-right\npass over the original string without re-scanning inserted text.\n\n`render.md` prescribes: a placeholder is exactly `{{` + name + `}}` with name\nmatching `[a-z]+`; every placeholder is replaced by `ctx[name]`; a name absent\nfrom ctx yields the empty string; replacement is a single pass with inserted\nvalues never re-scanned; braces not forming such a placeholder are literal;\nno other transformation.\n\n## Per-probe determination table\n\n| # | template | context | render.md prescribes | render.py output | determined? | agree? |\n|---|----------|---------|----------------------|------------------|-------------|--------|\n| 0 | `hello {{name}}` | name=ada | substitute `{{name}}` → `ada` | `hello ada` | yes | yes |\n| 1 | `{{a}}-{{b}}` | a=1, b=2 | substitute both placeholders | `1-2` | yes | yes |\n| 2 | `missing: {{ghost}}!` | {} | name not in ctx → empty string | `missing: !` | yes | yes |\n| 3 | `{{x}}{{x}}` | x=ab | \"replaces every placeholder\", incl. repeats/adjacency | `abab` | yes | yes |\n| 4 | `literal {{ name }} stays` | name=z | ` name ` contains spaces, not `[a-z]+` → not a placeholder → literal | `literal {{ name }} stays` | yes | yes |\n| 5 | `value {{v}}` | v=`{{w}}`, w=n | single pass; inserted value literal, never re-scanned → `{{w}}` stays | `value {{w}}` | yes | yes |\n| 6 | `{{}} empty` | {} | empty name fails `[a-z]+` (one or more required) → literal | `{{}} empty` | yes | yes |\n| 7 | `{{num1}}` | num1=x | `num1` contains a digit, not `[a-z]+` → not a placeholder → literal | `{{num1}}` | yes | yes |\n| 8 | `no placeholders` | a=b | no placeholders; \"no other transformation\" → unchanged | `no placeholders` | yes | yes |\n| 9 | `{{a}} and {{missing}} and {{b}}` | a=A, b=B | substitute a, b; missing → empty string | `A and  and B` | yes | yes |\n\n(Probe 9's output contains a double space: `and ` + `` + ` and`.)\n\n## Behavior classes exercised, with regex-level agreement argument\n\n1. **Well-formed placeholder substitution** (0, 1, 3, 9): `render.md` bullets 1\n   (\"replaces every placeholder with ctx[name]\"); `render.py`'s pattern\n   `\\{\\{([a-z]+)\\}\\}` matches exactly the spec's placeholder form and\n   substitutes `ctx[name]`. Adjacent and repeated placeholders (probe 3) are\n   covered by \"every placeholder\". Agreement.\n2. **Missing name → empty string** (2, 9): spec bullet 2; implemented by\n   `ctx.get(name, \"\")`. Agreement.\n3. **Malformed brace forms are literal** (4: internal spaces; 6: empty name;\n   7: digit in name): the spec defines names as `[a-z]+` and states that\n   anything else, \"including braces that do not form such a placeholder, is\n   literal text\". The regex cannot match any of these: a space, the empty\n   string, and `1` all fall outside `[a-z]`, and `\\}\\}` must immediately\n   follow the `[a-z]+` run (in `{{num1}}` the run `num` is followed by `1`,\n   and no other `{{` occurs), so `re.sub` leaves each string unchanged.\n   Agreement.\n4. **Single pass, no re-scanning of inserted values** (5): spec bullet 3 is\n   explicit; `re.sub` scans only the original template and, because the\n   replacement is a lambda, inserts its return value literally — `{{w}}`\n   survives to the output. Agreement.\n5. **No other transformation** (8, and all residual text in every probe):\n   spec bullet 4; `re.sub` copies non-matching text verbatim. Agreement.\n\n## Explicit argument that no undetermined or divergent behavior exists on this probe set\n\nThe five classes above exhaustively partition every behavior the ten probes\nexercise: each character of each template is either part of a well-formed\nplaceholder (class 1, with the missing-name sub-case class 2), part of a\nmalformed brace form (class 3), or plain literal text (class 5); the only\nprobe whose context value could interact with re-scanning is probe 5\n(class 4). For each class a specific clause of `render.md` fixes the output\nuniquely (no clause is silent on any class, and no two clauses conflict), and\nin each case the fixed output equals `render.py`'s output as shown in the\ntable. Potential underdetermination points that would need flagging —\noverlapping brace runs such as `{{{a}}}`, non-string context values (where\n`render.py` applies `str()` but the spec assumes string values), templates\nwhere a replacement could abut braces to form a new placeholder under a\nre-scanning reading — are not exercised by any probe: every context value in\n`probes.json` is a string, no template contains a brace run other than exact\n`{{`/`}}` pairs, and probe 5 is governed by the spec's explicit single-pass\nclause. Therefore the list of behaviors on this probe set that `render.md`\nleaves undetermined or determines differently from `render.py` is **empty**.\n\n**Conclusion (E-A):** `undetermined_behaviors = []`; the spec-prescribed\noutput equals `render.py`'s output on all ten probes.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":990,"cache_read_input_tokens":44389,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":990},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ee44e816-8bb9-4019-aa9a-8d0e6363eca5","uuid":"ceda2485-6d00-4f62-a327-ab05aa2bff6d","timestamp":"2026-08-09T17:17:36.539Z","request_id":"req_011CdsYytKEUrRhpDwxRnSz5"}
