{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_011CdsZEnCoHPm7uMNyPrWmw","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Stage S6 is complete. This trial's harness is the `isolated-child` family, so I executed the two in-session nodes (`observe-evidence`, `propose-child`) and left validation, launch, and integration to the root harness.\n\n**What I found and did:**\n\n- **Q1 (RESOLVED in-session):** I wrote `ea-analysis.md`, a per-probe analysis of all ten probes. render.md determines every behavior the probe set exercises, and every determination agrees with render.py — including the tricky cases: `{{ name }}`, `{{}}`, and `{{num1}}` are all malformed under the `[a-z]+` name rule and stay literal in both spec and code; a missing name yields the empty string; and probe 5's inserted `{{w}}` survives because both the spec's single-pass clause and `re.sub` with a lambda replacement forbid re-scanning. The analysis includes the explicit exhaustiveness argument E-A demands, so `undetermined_behaviors = []`.\n- **Q2 (UNRESOLVED, delegated):** E-B requires an author who has never accessed render.py — I'm disqualified by having read the package. I authored the full clean-room child bundle under `child/`: an attenuated contract (within `K-E6-child-max`), the harness from the template, a standalone prompt, an input manifest containing **only** `package/artifacts/render.md` (no render.py, no probes, no analysis of mine), and `integration-plan.json` with role `clean_room_implementer`.\n- **Q3/Q4 (UNRESOLVED, rule pre-committed):** The integration plan carries a judgment-free rule: run render.py and the child's `render_clean.py` on each of the ten probes, take the sorted differing indices as `divergent_probe_indices`, and set the verdict to DIVERGES iff that list is non-empty, else REPRODUCES.\n- **Deliverables written:** `result.json` (verdict and indices `PENDING-INTEGRATION`, `undetermined_behaviors: []`), `resolution.json`, `evidence.json`, `result-pending.json`, and `execution-ledger.jsonl` with the two node events plus one creator bookkeeping event — no `complete` event and no events for root-executed nodes.\n\nOne note: `child-templates/` contained only contract and harness templates (found by probing filenames, since I have no directory-listing tool); the prompt, manifest, and integration plan were authored directly to the shapes protocol.md specifies. Based on my own (non-authoritative) E-A analysis, I'd expect the child's comparison to come back empty and the final verdict to be REPRODUCES, but that determination belongs to root integration."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1218,"cache_read_input_tokens":63374,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1218},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ee44e816-8bb9-4019-aa9a-8d0e6363eca5","uuid":"756dd2c2-e914-47d1-ad43-22f6d6220c9b","timestamp":"2026-08-09T17:19:10.916Z","request_id":"req_011CdsZEikgSNbbYSLYGF89k"}
